<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly residue down, distillates up.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly residue down, distillates up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks fell by 954,000 barrels in the week ended December 18 to 9.049 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks rose by 469,000 barrels to 6.67 million barrels. Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Light distillate stocks also rose by 623,000 barrels to 5.419 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha. -- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
